---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import styles from '../styles/legal.module.css';
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Use | WitrQuran"
  description="Terms of Use for WitrQuran, a free and open source Quran listening platform."
  noindex={true}
>
  <div class={styles.pageContainer}>
    <nav class={styles.breadcrumb} aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span>/</span>
      <span>Terms of Use</span>
    </nav>

    <header class={styles.header}>
      <h1 class={styles.title}>Terms of Use</h1>
      <p class={styles.lastUpdated}>Last Updated: September 27, 2026</p>
    </header>

    <div class={styles.content}>
      <p>Welcome to WitrQuran</p>

      <p>WitrQuran is a free and open source Quran listening platform created to provide a simple fast and uninterrupted listening experience</p>

      <p>By accessing or using WitrQuran you agree to these Terms of Use</p>

      <p>If you do not agree with these terms please do not use the website</p>

      <h2>1. About WitrQuran</h2>

      <p>WitrQuran is an independent open source project created and maintained by <strong>Md Faruk Abdulla</strong></p>

      <p>The purpose of WitrQuran is to make listening to the Quran simple accessible and free from unnecessary distractions</p>

      <p>The Quran is the Book of Almighty Allah SWT</p>

      <p>WitrQuran does not claim to create author or own the Quran</p>

      <p>The platform is simply a tool created to make listening easier for everyone by the will of Allah SWT</p>

      <h2>2. Free Access</h2>

      <p>WitrQuran is completely free to use</p>

      <p>There are:</p>

      <ul>
        <li>No paid subscriptions</li>
        <li>No paid features</li>
        <li>No required accounts</li>
        <li>No registration fees</li>
        <li>No mandatory donations</li>
      </ul>

      <p>You may use the website for its intended purpose without creating an account or providing personal information</p>

      <h2>3. Permitted Use</h2>

      <p>You may use WitrQuran for lawful personal and non-commercial purposes including:</p>

      <ul>
        <li>Listening to Quran recitations</li>
        <li>Using the website for personal Quran study</li>
        <li>Sharing the WitrQuran website with others</li>
        <li>Accessing the publicly available open source code</li>
        <li>Contributing to the project through GitHub</li>
      </ul>

      <p>You must not use WitrQuran in a way that violates applicable laws or attempts to interfere with the operation or security of the website</p>

      <h2>4. No Account Required</h2>

      <p>WitrQuran does not currently provide user accounts</p>

      <p>You are not required to create an account provide a password or submit personal information to listen to the Quran</p>

      <h2>5. Open Source Software</h2>

      <p>The WitrQuran source code is publicly available on GitHub</p>

      <p>The software is released under the <strong>MIT License</strong></p>

      <p>The MIT License governs the use modification distribution and other rights relating to the WitrQuran source code</p>

      <p>These Terms of Use do not replace or modify the MIT License</p>

      <p><a href="https://github.com/witrfaruk/WitrQuran?utm_source" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View WitrQuran on GitHub</a></p>

      <p><a href="https://github.com/witrfaruk/WitrQuran/blob/main/LICENSE?utm_source" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View the MIT License</a></p>

      <h2>6. Quran Content and Audio</h2>

      <p>The Quran is the Book of Almighty Allah SWT</p>

      <p>WitrQuran provides access to Quranic Arabic audio for listening</p>

      <p>The Quran itself is not created or authored by WitrQuran</p>

      <p>WitrQuran also does not claim ownership of third-party recitation recordings made available through the platform</p>

      <p>Where applicable the rights and attribution associated with third-party content remain with their respective owners</p>

      <p>For additional information please see our <strong><a href="/copyright">Copyright &amp; Content Policy</a></strong></p>

      <h2>7. Third-Party Services</h2>

      <p>WitrQuran may rely on external infrastructure and services to operate and deliver the website and audio</p>

      <p>These may include services such as Cloudflare Vercel and external audio or content services</p>

      <p>Those services may have their own terms privacy policies and technical requirements</p>

      <p>WitrQuran is not responsible for the independent policies or practices of third-party services</p>

      <h2>8. Availability</h2>

      <p>We aim to keep WitrQuran available fast and reliable</p>

      <p>However we do not guarantee that the website will always be:</p>

      <ul>
        <li>Available</li>
        <li>Error free</li>
        <li>Uninterrupted</li>
        <li>Compatible with every device or browser</li>
        <li>Free from temporary technical problems</li>
      </ul>

      <p>The website may occasionally be modified updated suspended or temporarily unavailable for maintenance or other technical reasons</p>

      <h2>9. Accuracy and Content</h2>

      <p>WitrQuran is designed primarily as a Quran listening platform</p>

      <p>We make reasonable efforts to maintain the platform and its content correctly</p>

      <p>However technical errors interruptions or inaccuracies may occur</p>

      <p>If you identify an issue please report it through our designated reporting channel so that it can be reviewed</p>

      <h2>10. No Religious Authority</h2>

      <p>WitrQuran is a listening platform</p>

      <p>It does not provide:</p>

      <ul>
        <li>Fatwas</li>
        <li>Religious rulings</li>
        <li>Islamic legal advice</li>
        <li>Personalized religious guidance</li>
        <li>Scholarly interpretation</li>
      </ul>

      <p>Nothing on WitrQuran should be understood as replacing qualified Islamic scholarship</p>

      <h2>11. Intellectual Property</h2>

      <p>The WitrQuran software is open source under the MIT License</p>

      <p>Other materials available through WitrQuran including third-party audio recordings may be subject to separate intellectual property rights</p>

      <p>You may not assume that every piece of content available through the platform is owned by WitrQuran or covered by the MIT License</p>

      <p>If you believe content infringes your rights please contact us through the designated contact channel</p>

      <h2>12. Prohibited Activities</h2>

      <p>You must not:</p>

      <ul>
        <li>Attempt to disrupt or damage WitrQuran</li>
        <li>Attempt to gain unauthorized access to systems or services</li>
        <li>Abuse or overload the website</li>
        <li>Circumvent security measures</li>
        <li>Use automated systems in a manner that harms the service</li>
        <li>Use WitrQuran for unlawful purposes</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>13. External Links</h2>

      <p>WitrQuran may contain links to external websites or services</p>

      <p>These websites are operated independently and may have their own terms and privacy policies</p>

      <p>We are not responsible for the content availability security or practices of external websites</p>

      <h2>14. Privacy</h2>

      <p>Your use of WitrQuran is also subject to our <strong><a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a></strong> and <strong><a href="/cookies">Cookie Policy</a></strong></p>

      <p>WitrQuran is designed to minimize data collection and does not require user accounts</p>

      <h2>15. Changes to WitrQuran</h2>

      <p>We may modify improve or discontinue parts of WitrQuran at any time</p>

      <p>We may also update these Terms of Use when the service changes or when necessary for legal or operational reasons</p>

      <p>The updated version will be published on this page with a revised <strong>Last Updated</strong> date</p>

      <h2>16. Limitation of Liability</h2>

      <p>To the extent permitted by applicable law WitrQuran and its creator shall not be liable for indirect incidental consequential or other losses arising from your use of or inability to use the website</p>

      <p>WitrQuran is provided on an <strong>as-is</strong> and <strong>as-available</strong> basis without guarantees that the service will always be uninterrupted or error free</p>

      <p>Nothing in these Terms limits any rights or protections that cannot legally be excluded under applicable law</p>

      <h2>17. Governing Law</h2>

      <p>These Terms shall be interpreted and applied in accordance with applicable laws</p>

      <p>Where a specific jurisdiction is legally required the applicable mandatory laws of that jurisdiction will apply</p>

      <h2>18. Contact</h2>

      <p>For questions regarding these Terms of Use contact:</p>

      <p><strong>Md Faruk Abdulla</strong></p>

      <p><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:witrfaruk@proton.me">witrfaruk@proton.me</a></p>

      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://www.instagram.com/witrfaruk?utm_source" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Instagram</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/witrfaruk?utm_source" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn</a></li>
      </ul>

      <p>For technical issues and contributions:</p>

      <p><a href="https://github.com/witrfaruk/WitrQuran?utm_source" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">WitrQuran GitHub Repository</a></p>

      <p><strong>The Quran is from Almighty Allah SWT. WitrQuran is simply a tool created to make listening easier for everyone by His will.</strong></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
